       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 15 g/day is a potentially lethal dose. It carries a high risk of acute liver failure, and I know of no clinical scenario where it is therapeutic. You haven't given a rationale that would change that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range**, such as 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day max). Tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Enter it with a note** if there's a specific reason for the dose, such as a unit or formulation issue or a toxicology-directed protocol. I'd still want the dose to match a recognized regimen.\n- **Escalate through pharmacy.** If you believe this dose is warranted, a pharmacist or toxicology consult can verify it and enter it through the appropriate override pathway.\n\nIf the goal is stronger analgesia than 4 g/day of acetaminophen provides, I can help enter an adjunct instead, such as an NSAID or an opioid, at doses you specify."
      }
